# Project Overview

## Project Summary
- **Objective:** Migrate legacy SOAP API architecture to modern REST + Event Streaming stack to enable real-time data integration and reduce integration complexity from 4 weeks to 1 week per new consumer.
- **Strategic alignment:** Supports "Modernize Legacy Systems" 2026 priority; enables "Real-Time Analytics" product roadmap
- **Success criteria:**
  1. All 12 consumers migrated to REST (zero on SOAP by month 6)
  2. Integration time reduced to ≤7 days for new consumers
  3. Production incidents reduced from 2-3/month to <0.5/month
  4. Real-time data flows operational (sub-5-min latency)
- **Project lead:** [Your name], Platform Architecture Lead
- **Sponsor/Executive owner:** VP Engineering

## Key Dates
| Milestone | Planned | Status |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| Kickoff | 2026-08-12 | Planning |
| Phase 1 complete (Infrastructure) | 2026-10-07 | |
| Phase 2 complete (Build REST APIs) | 2026-11-18 | |
| Phase 3 complete (Pilot migration) | 2026-12-30 | |
| Phase 4 complete (Full rollout) | 2027-01-27 | |
| Closure (Bridge layer only) | 2027-01-27 | |

---

# Scope & Context

## What's In Scope
- Migrate 12 external SOAP API consumers to REST
- Deploy Kafka event streaming infrastructure
- Build REST API gateway with OAuth 2.0
- Create bridge layer for 12-month coexistence
- Document all APIs and migration processes
- Train all consumer teams

## What's Out of Scope
- Internal APIs (those are separate modernization effort)
- Mobile API changes
- Analytics pipeline rewrite (uses new APIs but owned by Analytics team)
- SOAP stack cleanup beyond decommissioning (can be future work)

## Assumptions
- All 12 consumers will have capacity to migrate (if not, will extend timeline)
- Kafka managed service will be sufficient (not self-managed)
- OAuth 2.0 will be approved by security (confirmed in proposal review)
- No breaking changes to data contracts (we maintain compatibility)
- External vendors will cooperate (most have REST SDK available)

