# Project Phases & Execution Plan

## Phase 1: Planning & Infrastructure Setup (Weeks 1-8 | Aug 12 - Oct 7)

### Work Stream 1: REST API Design & Standards
- **Deliverables:**
  - REST API design guidelines (versioning, naming, error handling)
  - OAuth 2.0 implementation spec
  - API security architecture document
- **Owner:** Technical Architect
- **Dependencies:** Security team approval of OAuth spec (from proposal review)
- **Success criteria:**
  - Design document reviewed and approved by tech steering committee
  - Security team sign-off on OAuth implementation
  - All consumer teams can review and provide feedback

### Work Stream 2: Kafka Infrastructure
- **Deliverables:**
  - Kafka cluster deployed (staging + production)
  - Event schema registry setup
  - Monitoring and alerting configured
  - Disaster recovery plan documented
- **Owner:** Infrastructure Lead
- **Dependencies:** Cloud infrastructure provisioned; Kafka expert consultant available
- **Success criteria:**
  - Kafka cluster handles 2x production load in staging
  - All monitoring dashboards operational
  - DR testing successful (can restore from backup)

### Work Stream 3: Bridge Layer Architecture
- **Deliverables:**
  - Bridge layer design (how SOAP calls route to REST internally)
  - Dual-write strategy documented
  - Rollback plan for each consumer
- **Owner:** Technical Architect + Backend engineers
- **Dependencies:** REST API design finalized
- **Success criteria:**
  - Design allows zero-downtime transition for each consumer
  - Team can explain dual-write guarantees

### Work Stream 4: Migration Playbook & Consumer Communication
- **Deliverables:**
  - Playbook for each consumer type (cloud, on-prem, hybrid)
  - FAQ document
  - Webinar for all consumer teams
  - Migration timeline per consumer
- **Owner:** Developer Advocate + Project Lead
- **Dependencies:** REST API design finalized; list of consumers confirmed
- **Success criteria:**
  - Each consumer team has clear migration path
  - Adoption feedback positive (NPS of migrate playbook >7)

### Phase Gate
- **Gate criteria:**
  - ✅ API design approved
  - ✅ Kafka infrastructure operational
  - ✅ Bridge layer design validated
  - ✅ All consumer teams have migration playbook + timeline
- **Gate approver:** VP Engineering
- **Target gate date:** 2026-10-07

---

## Phase 2: Build & Test REST APIs (Weeks 9-16 | Oct 8 - Nov 18)

### Work Stream 1: Implement REST APIs
- **Deliverables:**
  - REST versions of top 5 SOAP endpoints
  - API documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI)
  - Code committed to main branch with feature flags
- **Owner:** Backend Engineers (both)
- **Dependencies:** Phase 1 gate complete; API design finalized
- **Success criteria:**
  - Code review: 2 approvals minimum
  - Test coverage: >80% for all new code
  - Documentation: Each endpoint has examples and error cases

### Work Stream 2: Performance & Load Testing
- **Deliverables:**
  - Load test results (peak load = 2x production)
  - Performance tuning applied
  - Baseline metrics documented
- **Owner:** QA Lead + Backend engineers
- **Dependencies:** REST API implementation complete
- **Success criteria:**
  - p50 latency: <50ms, p95: <100ms, p99: <200ms
  - Can handle 2x production load without degradation
  - All metrics meet SLA requirements

### Work Stream 3: Security Testing
- **Deliverables:**
  - OAuth 2.0 flow validation
  - Security scan results (no critical findings)
  - Penetration test report (if required by security team)
- **Owner:** Security team (external); coordination by Technical Architect
- **Dependencies:** REST API implementation complete
- **Success criteria:**
  - Security sign-off received
  - No critical or high vulnerabilities

### Phase Gate
- **Gate criteria:**
  - ✅ 3 pilot consumers ready to test
  - ✅ Performance targets met
  - ✅ Security sign-off received
  - ✅ Documentation complete
- **Gate approver:** VP Engineering
- **Target gate date:** 2026-11-18

---

## Phase 3: Pilot Migration (Weeks 17-24 | Nov 19 - Dec 30)

### Work Stream 1: Migrate Pilot Consumers (3 customers)
- **Deliverables:**
  - Consumer A: Migrated to REST, bridge layer active, zero data loss
  - Consumer B: Migrated to REST, bridge layer active, zero data loss
  - Consumer C: Migrated to REST, bridge layer active, zero data loss
- **Owner:** Backend engineers + Integration lead
- **Dependencies:** Phase 2 gate complete; pilot consumers committed
- **Success criteria:**
  - All 3 consumers successfully sending/receiving via REST
  - Data validation: 100% data parity between old/new paths
  - Integration time: 1-2 weeks per consumer (from 4 weeks)

### Work Stream 2: Monitor & Tune
- **Deliverables:**
  - Weekly status reports to pilot consumers
  - Performance tuning applied based on real data
  - Incident response (if any)
- **Owner:** Infrastructure Lead + Backend engineers
- **Dependencies:** Pilot consumers live
- **Success criteria:**
  - Zero data loss incidents
  - <1 incident per consumer over 4 weeks
  - Performance meets targets

### Work Stream 3: Gather Feedback & Iterate
- **Deliverables:**
  - Feedback from 3 pilot consumers documented
  - Playbook updated based on learnings
  - Known issues and workarounds documented
- **Owner:** Developer Advocate
- **Dependencies:** Pilot consumers live for 2+ weeks
- **Success criteria:**
  - Playbook improved based on feedback
  - Next wave of consumers has higher confidence

### Phase Gate
- **Gate criteria:**
  - ✅ All 3 pilots successful (zero data loss, meets SLAs)
  - ✅ Integration time reduced to 1-2 weeks per consumer
  - ✅ Playbook updated; team confident in next wave
  - ✅ No critical issues remaining
- **Gate approver:** VP Engineering
- **Target gate date:** 2026-12-30

---

## Phase 4: Full Rollout & Decommission (Weeks 25-28 | Jan 1 - Jan 27, 2027)

### Work Stream 1: Migrate Remaining Consumers (9 customers)
- **Deliverables:**
  - 9 remaining consumers migrated to REST (one per week)
  - Bridge layer supporting all consumers
- **Owner:** Integration team
- **Dependencies:** Phase 3 complete; playbook proven
- **Success criteria:**
  - 12/12 consumers now on REST API
  - Zero unplanned downtime during migrations

### Work Stream 2: Decommission SOAP Stack
- **Deliverables:**
  - SOAP endpoints removed from production
  - Infrastructure decommissioned
  - Documentation archived
- **Owner:** Infrastructure Lead
- **Dependencies:** All consumers migrated
- **Success criteria:**
  - No traffic to SOAP endpoints
  - Infrastructure costs reduced (~$150K annually)

### Phase Gate
- **Gate criteria:**
  - ✅ All 12 consumers on REST
  - ✅ SOAP decommissioned
  - ✅ Savings realized
- **Gate approver:** VP Engineering
- **Target gate date:** 2027-01-27

